From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: Input: melfas_mip4 - do not log empty packets as errors (J701F local)

Written by Claude 2026-10-08 for the J701F project; not an upstream patch.
The MMS438 on this phone keeps its attention line low for a short time after
a packet is read. With the level-low trigger the vendor driver also uses, the
handler re-enters and reads a zero-length packet, which the driver reported
with dev_err thousands of times and pushed the boot log out of the ring
buffer. An edge trigger avoids the message but loses interrupts for good once
the line stays low (measured: one interrupt after boot, touch dead).
---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
@@ -605,7 +605,7 @@
 
 	/* Check size */
 	if (!size) {
-		dev_err(&client->dev, "Empty packet\n");
+		dev_dbg(&client->dev, "Empty packet\n");
 		goto out;
 	}
 
